- All 14 remaining sealed components classified from the drawing: market back prep room behind the x=1013 wall (2821), both checkstand lane banks (886+548), behind the Deli counter (809), the walled office block at the bank's east end (612), Restrooms (220), the two Cooking Connection demo-island interiors (154+107), the Deli block's service notch (70+55), and four ≤90-cell drafting slivers between abutting fixtures.
- 27 product labels probed across all wings (Cotton Balls, Dog Food, Coconut Water, Goya, Tortillas, Cough & Cold, Tobacco, …): every one lands *on* reachable floor, 0.00 m.
- Corridor-width map shows no red slivers; the pharmacy wedge exclusion strands no shelf labels (nearest product labels are east of x≈340).

**`data/28/walk_truth.json`**: 23 `must` (front alley incl. the fixed east segment, both entrance approaches, back alley, centre alley, five distinct aisle corridors spanning both wings, the badge alley, Dairy/Frozen/Deli/Floral/Pharmacy-pickup/Produce/Market/Meat Simple frontages, the café seating fix) and 18 `must_not` (outside/parking, two page corners, lease unit, pharmacy room, deli back + notch, both checkstand banks' lane interiors, restrooms, office block, market back room, both demo islands, NW back room, west sliver). Every coordinate was probed against the shipped `profile.npz`, and the lane-interior points were checked against an exclusion-free grid so they test the sealing rule rather than a fixture.

